# Code owners for Skillbox
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# This file routes review requests. It does not gate merges.
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" is deliberately left OFF in branch
# protection while this is a solo repository. GitHub never requests a review from
# the author of a pull request, and nobody can approve their own, so enabling it
# with a single code owner would make every pull request unmergeable except by
# administrator bypass. Turn it on when there is a second maintainer to review.
#
# CODEOWNERS only takes effect from the copy on the default branch, and only for
# owners who have write access to the repository.

* @ZacheryKuykendall

# Paths worth requiring extra review on once there is more than one maintainer.
# CODEOWNERS cannot express "extra" review by itself; that needs a branch
# protection rule. Listed here so the intent is not lost.
#
#   /packages/core/src/paths.ts        Security boundary: path containment
#   /packages/core/src/apply.ts        Filesystem mutation and rollback
#   /packages/core/src/lockfile.ts     Lockfile determinism
#   /docs/architecture/decisions/      Architectural decision records
#   /docs/architecture/security-model.md
#   /.gitattributes                    Line endings, which integrity digests depend on
